{"tool_name":"iq-tree","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","debian","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"iq-tree","home":"http://www.cibiv.at/software/iqtree/","summary":"Very efficient phylogenetic software for reconstructing maximum-likelihood trees and assessing branch supports with the ultrafast bootstrap approximation. It is based on the IQPNNI algorithm with 10-fold speedup together with substantially additional features.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:46:55Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:02:46.064218Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:iq-tree","credit":[{"email":"admin.vbc5@univie.ac.at","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.cibiv.at/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.iqtree.org/doc/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["eperezv"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Phylogenetic tree generation (maximum likelihood and Bayesian methods)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0547"}]}],"name":"IQ-TREE","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkw256","metadata":{"abstract":"This article presents W-IQ-TREE, an intuitive and user-friendly web interface and server for IQ-TREE, an efficient phylogenetic software for maximum likelihood analysis. W-IQ-TREE supports multiple sequence types (DNA, protein, codon, binary and morphology) in common alignment formats and a wide range of evolutionary models including mixture and partition models. W-IQ-TREE performs fast model selection, partition scheme finding, efficient tree reconstruction, ultrafast bootstrapping, branch tests, and tree topology tests. All computations are conducted on a dedicated computer cluster and the users receive the results via URL or email. W-IQ-TREE is available at http://iqtree.cibiv.univie.ac.at. It is free and open to all users and there is no login requirement.","authors":[{"name":"Minh B.Q."},{"name":"Nguyen L.-T."},{"nam